# My openElement App

Generated by [`@openelement/create`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@openelement/create).
A file-based openElement app: page routes live in `app/routes/`, compiled page
elements and shared style sheets in `app/components/`, and client islands
(including the `app-shell` layout island) in `app/islands/`.

This starter pins the exact `@openelement/element` and `@openelement/router`
versions it was generated from (`${v.element}`) in `deno.json`; update both
there when moving to a new release.

Styling ownership is split three ways. Global design tokens and the document
baseline (`body`, `::selection`) live in `vite.config.ts`
(`inject.headFragments`). Pages use light roots and own their rules in
`static styles` (`app/components/page-styles.ts`): the server inlines each
page's sheets into the SSR output as a `@scope(<page-tag>)` style block, so
pages are fully styled with zero client JavaScript. The shell and the islands
hydrate in the browser and carry their own `static styles`.

## Tasks

- `deno task dev` — start the Vite dev server.
- `deno task check` — type-check every route/component file. When you add a
  route file, add it to this task's file list in `deno.json`.
- `deno task test` — run Deno tests (the starter ships none).
- `deno task build` — production build (SSG + Nitro server) into `dist/`.
- `deno task start` — serve the production build. Use this for production
  preview: the starter ships a request-time route (`/contact`), so
  `deno task preview` (static-only preview, #601) is refused by design.
- `deno task preview` — static-only preview; refused for this starter (see
  above).

## Blog

Blog posts are compiled page routes: `app/routes/blog/welcome.tsx` renders at
`/blog/welcome`, prerendered at build time. Add a post by creating a page
element under `app/components/` and a route module under `app/routes/blog/`,
then link it from `app/routes/blog/index.tsx` (the index list is static
authoring). Interactive content belongs in a compiled island composed from
the page.

## Import map notes

`deno.json` maps `@openelement/router/nitro-mount` and `hono` even
though no source file imports them: the dev server and the production
build resolve `hono` when loading the generated server entry (the
bundled `dist/` output inlines it), and Nitro deployments bridge the
built handler through `@openelement/router/nitro-mount`. Do not remove
them.

## Brand assets

`public/openelement-mark.svg` is the openElement brand mark shipped with the
starter — use it for a favicon or page header, or delete it if unused.
